{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/21768-resonance-effect-on-werewolf","id":21768,"title":"Resonance effect on Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-02T11:02:01-08:00","id":21768,"title":"Resonance effect on Werewolf","content":"I'm wondering what is the effect for a Werewolf to get essence that is what we could assume as &quot;bad&quot; resonance. For example, my players have access to a locus of death in an hospital and if they start to gather the essence if they can take care of it's guardian, what would be the impact on them? I'm not really finding anything, but in the Manitou Springs demo, they have to cleanse the locus by dealing with the ghosts, saying at the end &quot;it is no longer tainted with a resonance of death.&quot; Is it just because spirits of death are more antagonist that let's say spirit of euphoria that a pack of Uratha would cleanse a locus from that &quot;bad&quot; resonance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1466-plabu","name":"Plabu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:29:34-08:00","id":21789,"title":"","content":"It's very brief, and I'm sure there's more, but <b>Lore of the Forsaken</b> (chapter 4) does mention that the resonance of the Essence can influence the Uratha just like the spirits, but doesn't really give a lot of details.<br /> <br /> For myself, I'd play it out as having a fraction of the same level of influence on the Urathas' as it would the spirits for the purposes of how they behave, but have the <i>same </i>amount of influence when it comes to the Gifts, Rites, etc that are <i>fueled </i>by that Essence.<br /> <br /> As far as who's more antagonistic, that's not so much of a problem as the Essence tainting the intentions of it's use. Death resonance is a lot harder to bend to the will of the Uratha than euphoria (unless the intent is to kill someone, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 12-02-2013, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T04:13:24-08:00","id":24279,"title":"","content":"In my chronicles, my players fought against winter spirit. The essence of the whole town was tainted with ice and cold. At the beginning, when they have used essence, they have felt a really cold sensation. At the end, they could have one arm or leg frozen and covered of ice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1549-obiwankennedy","name":"ObiWanKennedy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T05:15:18-08:00","id":24300,"title":"","content":"In the Forsaken chronicler's guide (not sure which part) it does suggest that resonance does more to werewolves who absorb it. I remember a description of someone eating a bulldozer spirit turning yellowish and getting a wide, flattened forehead.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you could at least do it like Changeling is meant to, there when you absorb glamour from certain emotions, it's tainted with that emotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:41:11-08:00","id":24553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/21768-resonance-effect-on-werewolf?p=24300#post24300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Forsaken chronicler's guide (not sure which part) it does suggest that resonance does more to werewolves who absorb it. I remember a description of someone eating a bulldozer spirit turning yellowish and getting a wide, flattened forehead.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you could at least do it like Changeling is meant to, there when you absorb glamour from certain emotions, it's tainted with that emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's under the <b>Spirit Predation</b> part, sub-section <i>Bonuses from Essence</i>. Not as relevant to this topic as I hoped when I went looking for it, but it would be a good base to go from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- I